{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02127",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.28,
      "end_seconds": 7.62,
      "duration_seconds": 6.34,
      "text": "Let me think, hello, doctor. I think it's my turn."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 9.15,
      "end_seconds": 13.98,
      "duration_seconds": 4.83,
      "text": "Yes, come in and and sit down. What brings you here today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 15.99,
      "end_seconds": 26.72,
      "duration_seconds": 10.73,
      "text": "Doctor, um, I'm just here to help with the details. Um, he's been having not listening at school, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 27.93,
      "end_seconds": 31.27,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "How many days or weeks has it been?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 32.35,
      "end_seconds": 42.63,
      "duration_seconds": 10.28,
      "text": "it's been going on for about two weeks. I took the morning off to come in today"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 43.03,
      "end_seconds": 46.62,
      "duration_seconds": 3.59,
      "text": "Right, right. Is there anything else with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 48.31,
      "end_seconds": 76.98,
      "duration_seconds": 28.67,
      "text": "A cold that won't go goes along with it, most of the time. The cold that won't go? That's been for about a month. Let me think, and there's not hearing very well as well, one week now. Uh, and I've been turning the television up as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 78.13,
      "end_seconds": 83.59,
      "duration_seconds": 5.46,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any discharge, ear pain or fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 84.31,
      "end_seconds": 89.7,
      "duration_seconds": 5.39,
      "text": "Right, no discharge, ear pain or fever, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 90.67,
      "end_seconds": 92.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "And dizziness, any of that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 93.47,
      "end_seconds": 96.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "Not at all, no dizziness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 97.37,
      "end_seconds": 98.78,
      "duration_seconds": 1.41,
      "text": "Neurologically, anything strange?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 99.36,
      "end_seconds": 101.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.12,
      "text": "No, that's all normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 102.94,
      "end_seconds": 107.54,
      "duration_seconds": 4.6,
      "text": "Any inherited conditions that you know of in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 108.42,
      "end_seconds": 112.94,
      "duration_seconds": 4.52,
      "text": "Hmm, my mother has an underactive thyroid."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 124.21,
      "end_seconds": 129.29,
      "duration_seconds": 5.08,
      "text": "Are you allergic to anything? Any allergies to medicines or foods?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 130.58,
      "end_seconds": 135.46,
      "duration_seconds": 4.88,
      "text": "Hmm, I don't think I have any, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 136.57,
      "end_seconds": 144.31,
      "duration_seconds": 7.74,
      "text": "actually, I'm not sure that's right i seem to recall a problem with naproxen"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 145.01,
      "end_seconds": 149.72,
      "duration_seconds": 4.71,
      "text": "Uh, you know, I don't remember that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 151.18,
      "end_seconds": 156.57,
      "duration_seconds": 5.39,
      "text": "Okay, I'll note both of those. Any surgery in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 158.51,
      "end_seconds": 164.2,
      "duration_seconds": 5.69,
      "text": "Just a meniscus repair on my knee, four years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 170.15,
      "end_seconds": 174.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "do you take any prescribed or over-the-counter medicines?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 175.93,
      "end_seconds": 189.34,
      "duration_seconds": 13.41,
      "text": "Sorry, what was I saying, it's Tiotropium inhaler, once a day for my chest. I'm on alendronate, 70 milligrams, once a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 190.24,
      "end_seconds": 200.53,
      "duration_seconds": 10.29,
      "text": "doctor, um, I think the last prescription for the alendronate was 140 milligrams we changed it at the last visit"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 201.47,
      "end_seconds": 205.27,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "hm do you have the latest prescription with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 206.03,
      "end_seconds": 210.27,
      "duration_seconds": 4.24,
      "text": "I don't think I have it with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 226.85,
      "end_seconds": 231.41,
      "duration_seconds": 4.56,
      "text": "Let's talk a little about your daily life and and habits."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 232.91,
      "end_seconds": 243.39,
      "duration_seconds": 10.48,
      "text": "I'm a plumber, lots of bending and kneeling. My partner and our baby. Not much, I mostly stay in these days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 251.96,
      "end_seconds": 254.75,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "do you have any long-term conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 255.62,
      "end_seconds": 262.77,
      "duration_seconds": 7.15,
      "text": "I've got COPD. My sister suggested writing things down, but I forgot."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 263.59,
      "end_seconds": 264.66,
      "duration_seconds": 1.07,
      "text": "hm, okay"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 265.48,
      "end_seconds": 272.57,
      "duration_seconds": 7.09,
      "text": "Yes, thin bones. My family kept telling me to get it checked."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 273.15,
      "end_seconds": 275.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "I'll just record a few vital signs."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 288.6,
      "end_seconds": 291.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "Keep your arm relaxed for me..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 300.64,
      "end_seconds": 306.85,
      "duration_seconds": 6.21,
      "text": "Okay: respiratory rate 14, pressure 112 over 80, pulse is 82 beats a a minute."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 308.51,
      "end_seconds": 312.7,
      "duration_seconds": 4.19,
      "text": "I'd like to check you over now, if that's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 313.99,
      "end_seconds": 315.02,
      "duration_seconds": 1.03,
      "text": "That's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 316.28,
      "end_seconds": 319.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "Stay as you are for a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 328.06,
      "end_seconds": 332.44,
      "duration_seconds": 4.38,
      "text": "both ear drums look dull and retracted with fluid behind them"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 336.34,
      "end_seconds": 344.97,
      "duration_seconds": 8.63,
      "text": "Okay, that's enough for me. Taking everything into account, this is probably glue ear. Wax is also on my list."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 346.8,
      "end_seconds": 350.76,
      "duration_seconds": 3.96,
      "text": "Um, what are the odds it's serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 351.67,
      "end_seconds": 382.51,
      "duration_seconds": 30.84,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now glue ear is my leading thought, not anything worse. I'm sending you for a hearing test because of reduced hearing. We will watch for three months, and sit him at the front of the class. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 386.57,
      "end_seconds": 391.41,
      "duration_seconds": 4.84,
      "text": "okay, uh, I'll look out for that"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 392.42,
      "end_seconds": 398.22,
      "duration_seconds": 5.8,
      "text": "If the symptoms get worse, that's the point to come in urgently."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 398.95,
      "end_seconds": 402.53,
      "duration_seconds": 3.58,
      "text": "I, I know what to watch for."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 404.09,
      "end_seconds": 409.6,
      "duration_seconds": 5.51,
      "text": "let's review you in three months. That's all from me. Any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 411.53,
      "end_seconds": 414.72,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "I think I understand everything thanks"
    }
  ]
}